# Keep text files LF in the working tree, not only in the repository.
#
# Without this, a clone with core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) gets CRLF on
# checkout. That is usually harmless, but not here: the provenance graph stores multi-line
# Turtle literals - a SWRL rule's statement text is "# <name>\n<rule>" - and a CRLF
# checkout puts a stray \r inside the literal itself. The recorded text then no longer
# equals the text ttl_model.py derives from the ontology, and every rule reports as
# unmatched. The graph is fine; the checkout is what differs.
#
# It also keeps gsnprov:fileChecksum meaningful across platforms. tools/matching.py
# normalises line endings before hashing as well, so the two are belt and braces.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch these.
*.xlsx  binary
*.xls   binary
*.docx  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
